diff --git a/audit/FINDINGS.md b/audit/FINDINGS.md
index d1e3922..1edc5e6 100644
--- a/audit/FINDINGS.md
+++ b/audit/FINDINGS.md
@@ -1166,3 +1166,91 @@ The collector needs to sort by `width` descending and exclude descendants of
 `#mobile-sheet` before the next run. Until then, **do not guess the cause** —
 every entry currently visible in the offender list is a `width: 100%` element
 stretched by an already-wide document, i.e. a consequence.
+
+---
+
+## 15. Second measurement pass — what moved, and one instrument correction
+
+Same harness, same 220 cells, after patches 06, 07C and 10.
+
+| | run 1 | run 2 |
+|---|---|---|
+| axe violations | **220 cells** | **133 cells** |
+| form control under 16px | 6 | **0** |
+| `aria-hidden-focus` | 201 cells | **0** |
+| `document-title` / `html-has-lang` | 19 each | **0** |
+| horizontal overflow | 16 | 16 (untouched until now) |
+
+Remaining axe rules, in full: `color-contrast` **x133** and `target-size` **x8**.
+Nothing else fires.
+
+`document-title` and `html-has-lang` disappearing confirms the F-34 withdrawal
+was right: the page was always fine, and `waitUntil: 'networkidle'` was the bug —
+`/register` polls `/api/auth/session` continuously, so the wait returned at an
+arbitrary point and axe evaluated a half-built document.
+
+### F-35 · The overflow on every service-area page is one CTA button · **P0**
+
+With the collector ranking by intrinsic width instead of DOM order, the cause is
+unambiguous:
+
+| Route | widest non-full element | width | document |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `/service-areas/downtown-toronto` | `a.btn.btn-copper.btn-lg` | **493px** | 513 |
+| `/service-areas` | `a.btn.btn-copper.btn-lg` | **339px** | 359 |
+| `/` | `a.btn.btn-copper` | 308px | 330 |
+| `/products/floorforge` | `div.reveal` | 138px | 324 |
+
+493 + 20px shell padding = 513, exactly the document width. 339 + 20 = 359,
+exactly. The button *is* the document.
+
+`.btn` carried `white-space: nowrap`, so every CTA is as wide as its label — and
+the labels are not short:
+
+- `service-areas/page.tsx:38` — "Book your free in-home estimate"
+- `service-areas/[city]/page.tsx:152` — "Get your fixed-price estimate in {city.name}",
+  which on `downtown-toronto` renders "…in Toronto · Downtown"
+
+That also explains why the excess tracked the viewport perfectly (320 → +193,
+430 → +83, all summing to 513): a fixed-width element on a variable viewport.
+
+`nowrap` was there to keep the icon and arrow on one line, which `inline-flex`
+already does. Replaced with `white-space: normal`, `text-wrap: balance`,
+`max-width: 100%`, and `line-height: 1` → `1.2` because a button that can wrap
+needs leading.
+
+### The tap-target metric was mine, and it was wrong
+
+Run 1 reported 201 of 220 cells. After the footer fix, run 2 reported **220** —
+worse. That is not a regression in the site.
+
+The checker required **≥ 44px on both axes**. Giving footer links a 44px
+min-height made `a "Terms"` measure **41 × 44** — correct height, and now failing
+a 44px *width* test. **No standard asks a text link to be 44px wide.**
+
+- **WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8 (AA)** asks 24 × 24 CSS px, or adequate spacing.
+- **Apple HIG** asks 44 × 44, which is the right bar for controls with **no
+  text** — icon buttons, toggles — where there is nothing else to aim at.
+
+axe's own `target-size` rule, which implements the actual criterion, fires on
+**8 cells**, both themes of `/`. That is the real number; 220 was an artefact.
+
+The collector now reports three separate figures — `tapBelowWcag` (< 24px, a
+real failure), `tapSmall` (icon-only control < 44px, HIG advisory), and
+`tapShort` (text control under 44px tall, informational) — so a genuine failure
+can never be buried in advisory noise again.
+
+**Lesson: when a metric moves the wrong way after a fix that was verified in the
+code, suspect the metric.** Run 1's 201 was not wrong about the footer — it was
+wrong about how many of those 201 mattered.
+
+### Still open: `color-contrast` x133
+
+Routes: light `/`, `/products/floorforge`, `/authority`, `/technical-library`,
+`/blog`, `/case-studies`; dark `/`, `/authority`.
+
+Patch 07C fixed the `.tlx-*` text primitives and the dark-mode counts dropped,
+but `/technical-library` and `/blog` still fail in **light**, and `/` and
+`/authority` fail in both. Those are different namespaces from the ones already
+swept. The failing node HTML is needed before this can be fixed — inferring it
+from token tables is how F-33 got half-fixed the first time.
